        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "28-1. In our representative democracy, in which ultimate power is retained by the people and exercised through delegation of authority, the Board and the Association advocate the realization of the full potential of each individual by recognition of and respect for his-her dignity. It therefore follows that the education of each individual must develop the essential fundamental processes and those skills, understandings, and attitudes which will affect his-her harmonious development as a spiritual, intellectual, physical, emotional, and social being. It is recognized that these democratic values can best be transmitted in an atmosphere which is free from censorship and artificial restraints upon free inquiry and learning, and in which academic freedom for teacher and student is encouraged.",
